  urldate = {2026-04-07},
  abstract = {Electricity market models play a crucial role in addressing various research questions related to future electricity supply systems. As the energy transition progresses, the electricity market must evolve to incorporate renewable energy and demand-side flexibility while ensuring adequate investment incentives for reliable capacity. The design of electricity market models for future electricity markets requires a multifaceted approach that considers temporal, spatial, methodological, technical, and integrative criteria. A comprehensive review of 30 existing models identifies opportunities for advancement, particularly in the area of simulating the future electricity market. The analysis of these models indicates areas where improvements can be made in terms of realistic modeling. These areas include the modeling of human behavior, enhanced spatial resolution, representation of multiple electricity markets, and improved uncertainty modeling.},
